jqjs (https://github.com/mwh/jqjs) at f2894f6 — Lambda benchmark patch.
Applied to test/benchmark/text/jq/vendor/jqjs.js; see test/benchmark/text/jq/VENDOR.md.

1. Lexical environments. `conf` is never mutated: a call or an `as`/reduce/
   foreach binding derives a new one. A call's argument frame chains to the
   frame of the lexically enclosing def (not the caller's), and each argument
   is a closure over the caller's conf. Upstream grew the frame chain by one
   prototype link per active call (O(call depth) argument lookups, 79% of
   jq_bf's time) and evaluated arguments in the callee's scope (wrong results
   for e.g. recursive `def ack($m; $n)`).
2. Copy-on-write assignment. `|=` and `=` copy only the containers on each
   updated path, once per assignment, and read paths from the original input
   (jq's reduce-over-path(f) definition). Upstream deep-copied the whole input
   with JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...)) per assignment and re-walked it after.
3. Linear `add/0` for arrays and objects (upstream re-copied the running sum
   per element).

jq 1.7.1 tests/jq.test via run-test.js: 339 passed / 94 failed before,
341 / 92 after, no newly failing case.

